    "methods_description": "Electrodes were arranged in three rings (caudal, middle, cranial) around the neck, adapted from a prior spinal recording montage. Each trial consisted of an auditory cue followed by median nerve stimulation at the left wrist, with the cue-stimulus interval either fixed (1100 ms) or randomly varied (100-2100 ms) across alternating blocks. Some trials included a second stimulus (80 ms ISI) to create deviant trials. Subjects completed two sessions (days) with block order counterbalanced.",
